WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.998 --> 00:00:04.958
welcome to the Homeroom livestream.

00:00:04.958 --> 00:00:07.486
We have a very exciting
conversation planned,

00:00:07.486 --> 00:00:09.608
but before we dive into that,

00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:11.348
I'll give you my standard announcements.

00:00:11.348 --> 00:00:13.608
First of all, just a
reminder that Khan Academy

00:00:13.608 --> 00:00:16.028
is a not-for-profit organization

00:00:16.028 --> 00:00:18.768
and we wouldn't exist without
philanthropic donations

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:19.798
from folks like yourself.

00:00:19.798 --> 00:00:22.823
So if you have the time
and the generosity,

00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:25.573
please go to khanacademy.org/donate

00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:29.113
and gifts of all sizes
make a huge difference.

00:00:29.113 --> 00:00:31.355
I also want to give a special shout out

00:00:31.355 --> 00:00:33.778
to several organizations
that have stepped up

00:00:33.778 --> 00:00:35.328
over the last few months.

00:00:35.328 --> 00:00:37.018
Khan Academy was running
at a bit of a deficit

00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:38.918
even before COVID, and
then you can imagine,

00:00:38.918 --> 00:00:42.313
our traffic has been 2 to
3X of what it typically is.

00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:45.168
We've been trying to accelerate
a whole bunch of programs

00:00:45.168 --> 00:00:48.308
and content and ways to
support teachers and families,

00:00:48.308 --> 00:00:50.758
so special thanks to Bank
of America, Google.org,

00:00:50.758 --> 00:00:54.568
AT&amp;T, Fastly and Novartis
for helping us fill that gap.

00:00:54.568 --> 00:00:57.978
But we still are running a
gap, especially for next year.

00:00:57.978 --> 00:01:00.458
So any support that can be provided

00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:02.716
is very much appreciated.

00:01:02.716 --> 00:01:06.548
So, with that, I am very
excited to introduce

00:01:06.548 --> 00:01:08.319
our guest, Tom Inglesby,

00:01:08.319 --> 00:01:12.523
who's the director of the
Center for Health Security

00:01:12.523 --> 00:01:14.768
at Johns Hopkins University.

00:01:14.768 --> 00:01:16.024
Good to see you, Tom.

00:01:16.024 --> 00:01:17.758
- Great to be with you, Sal.

00:01:18.808 --> 00:01:20.468
- So health security seems to be

00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:22.395
a very relevant topic right now.

00:01:22.395 --> 00:01:23.228
(laughs)

00:01:23.228 --> 00:01:27.178
And maybe a good place to start, you know,

00:01:27.178 --> 00:01:30.248
I don't want to be flip about
a serious thing, you know,

00:01:30.248 --> 00:01:33.328
where are we in your mind
in this COVID journey?

00:01:33.328 --> 00:01:35.088
We're obviously six months in.

00:01:35.088 --> 00:01:36.968
People, you know, I
remember, back in March,

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.038
people kinda like were saying,

00:01:38.038 --> 00:01:39.798
maybe it's just going to
be for a month or two,

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:41.408
and then it's back to normal.

00:01:41.408 --> 00:01:43.588
Obviously, that hasn't been.

00:01:43.588 --> 00:01:44.888
How are you looking at it?

00:01:46.608 --> 00:01:50.188
- Yeah, I think, I mean, we're
in the middle, I would say.

00:01:50.188 --> 00:01:52.418
We're definitely not through it yet.

00:01:52.418 --> 00:01:55.598
I think in some places in the country,

00:01:55.598 --> 00:01:57.532
we're probably still at the very beginning

00:01:57.532 --> 00:02:00.218
because the number of people who have

00:02:00.218 --> 00:02:02.673
antibodies to the disease

00:02:02.673 --> 00:02:04.914
is very low in some places,

00:02:04.914 --> 00:02:07.923
particularly in counties
that aren't very populous.

00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:10.488
In some cities, they've
really gone through it,

00:02:10.488 --> 00:02:12.358
like New York city there
are some parts of the city

00:02:12.358 --> 00:02:15.148
which have really
experienced terrible disease,

00:02:15.148 --> 00:02:18.578
have maybe 40, 50% of the
people have been exposed,

00:02:18.578 --> 00:02:20.408
but that's a real exception.

00:02:20.408 --> 00:02:22.028
Most of the country hasn't been exposed.

00:02:22.028 --> 00:02:24.643
Most of the country is
still susceptible to this,

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:29.319
but the numbers are coming
down slowly in the last month,

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:31.460
and I'm cautiously optimistic

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.698
that if we continue to act in this way

00:02:34.698 --> 00:02:36.939
and don't completely change your behavior

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:39.558
once September starts that we could keep

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:43.121
moving in this direction until
hopefully we get a vaccine.

00:02:44.358 --> 00:02:45.848
- And before we jump into vaccines

00:02:45.848 --> 00:02:46.818
and even possible therapies,

00:02:46.818 --> 00:02:48.838
I would encourage everyone watching

00:02:48.838 --> 00:02:50.788
please put your questions on Facebook

00:02:50.788 --> 00:02:55.788
and the YouTube message boards
for both myself and Tom.

00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:58.978
I will ask as many of those
questions as possible.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.728
And we're gonna be
talking about, obviously,

00:03:00.728 --> 00:03:02.728
this COVID journey, vaccines, therapies,

00:03:02.728 --> 00:03:04.654
and also just how does that interface with

00:03:04.654 --> 00:03:05.868
how we live our life,

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:08.928
especially in things
like university campuses,

00:03:08.928 --> 00:03:10.883
which Tom is also expert on.

00:03:10.883 --> 00:03:13.578
Before I even jump into
the vaccine conversation,

00:03:13.578 --> 00:03:16.818
you mentioned at the level of
antibodies in the population

00:03:16.818 --> 00:03:17.858
being very important.

00:03:17.858 --> 00:03:22.397
Obviously, antibodies are
things that can tag pathogens

00:03:22.397 --> 00:03:24.098
as they come into the body

00:03:24.098 --> 00:03:26.448
so that your immune system
can respond to them.

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:30.938
Does COVID work the way
that many other things do?

00:03:30.938 --> 00:03:32.731
I've also read things that,
you know, people might think

00:03:32.731 --> 00:03:34.638
that the antibodies might not last,

00:03:34.638 --> 00:03:36.948
or they might not be as
robust as necessary to,

00:03:36.948 --> 00:03:38.801
even for someone who's had COVID,

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.140
you know, they might be
able to get it again.

00:03:43.111 --> 00:03:45.337
- We don't know enough
about it yet to say.

00:03:45.337 --> 00:03:48.070
I think that's an important,
very important point.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:52.208
We have some studies that say that

00:03:52.208 --> 00:03:56.568
people are protected at
least as long as four months,

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:59.048
but in practice we've seen, so far,

00:03:59.048 --> 00:04:02.858
very few repeat infections.

00:04:02.858 --> 00:04:05.328
So I think four months,
three to four months,

00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:08.346
is probably the minimum for most people.

00:04:08.346 --> 00:04:12.568
The maximum level of protection
might be pretty long,

00:04:12.568 --> 00:04:13.628
we just don't know yet.

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:16.098
We haven't had enough time to study it.

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:17.528
But it's a great point,

00:04:17.528 --> 00:04:19.288
we don't want to give
people the impression

00:04:19.288 --> 00:04:21.958
that just because their
antibody test is positive

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:24.251
that they should be fully confident

00:04:24.251 --> 00:04:26.366
that they are immune to it.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.916
We don't know that for sure.

00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:30.508
We do think it probably
provides protection,

00:04:30.508 --> 00:04:33.506
but we don't want to be overly confident

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:37.566
this early in the science of the response.

00:04:37.566 --> 00:04:39.508
- But that sounds quite hopeful.

00:04:39.508 --> 00:04:41.588
As you mentioned, there's very few cases,

00:04:41.588 --> 00:04:43.908
there are a few, but very few
cases of repeat infections,

00:04:43.908 --> 00:04:45.418
it seems like, at least four months.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.668
And you know, this is all
about your point earlier

00:04:47.668 --> 00:04:50.098
about the antibodies being a
sufficient number of people

00:04:50.098 --> 00:04:51.068
having them in a population,

00:04:51.068 --> 00:04:53.148
it's all about this herd
immunity at some point

00:04:53.148 --> 00:04:54.668
if enough people have it.

00:04:54.668 --> 00:04:56.728
So, going on to vaccines,
which is, I guess,

00:04:56.728 --> 00:05:00.038
one way of getting
people antibodies faster

00:05:00.038 --> 00:05:01.162
or in a broader way,

00:05:01.162 --> 00:05:03.268
where do you think we are on that journey?

00:05:03.268 --> 00:05:06.308
You know, you hear some places like Russia

00:05:06.308 --> 00:05:08.758
and I think we've heard out of China, too,

00:05:08.758 --> 00:05:12.508
that they've been administering
some form of a vaccine.

00:05:12.508 --> 00:05:13.848
There's talk in the US about

00:05:13.848 --> 00:05:15.898
potentially accelerating some of those.

00:05:15.898 --> 00:05:17.998
How do you think this
is going to play out?

00:05:17.998 --> 00:05:21.078
Do you think what we're
hearing out of Russia or China

00:05:21.078 --> 00:05:22.461
is real and credible,

00:05:22.461 --> 00:05:24.468
and do you think the US should accelerate

00:05:24.468 --> 00:05:25.478
those types of efforts,

00:05:25.478 --> 00:05:28.281
or do you think it's gonna
play out slightly slower?

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.598
- Yeah, I don't think we should accelerate

00:05:31.598 --> 00:05:32.758
what we're doing in the US.

00:05:32.758 --> 00:05:34.338
I think it's difficult to know

00:05:34.338 --> 00:05:35.878
what's going on in China and Russia

00:05:35.878 --> 00:05:37.038
because there's not a whole lot

00:05:37.038 --> 00:05:38.338
of information being provided

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:41.278
about how they're using
their vaccine candidates.

00:05:41.278 --> 00:05:42.312
I think Russia,

00:05:42.312 --> 00:05:44.648
there's a study that's come out

00:05:44.648 --> 00:05:49.648
that shows some early
evidence of blood markers

00:05:50.142 --> 00:05:52.128
of potential immunity,

00:05:52.128 --> 00:05:54.348
but we don't have any real clinical data,

00:05:54.348 --> 00:05:55.181
we don't have the results

00:05:55.181 --> 00:05:57.588
of clinical trials yet, from Russia,

00:05:57.588 --> 00:05:59.038
and the Chinese clinical trials

00:05:59.038 --> 00:05:59.918
we know some about,

00:05:59.918 --> 00:06:02.058
but we don't know enough about.

00:06:02.058 --> 00:06:03.388
So, they're presuming,

00:06:03.388 --> 00:06:05.145
if they, in truth, are actually beginning

00:06:05.145 --> 00:06:07.398
to vaccinate a lot of people,

00:06:07.398 --> 00:06:09.478
that is something we
wouldn't do in the US.

00:06:09.478 --> 00:06:12.208
We would proceed more cautiously.

00:06:12.208 --> 00:06:15.648
In the US the plan is to, right now,

00:06:15.648 --> 00:06:17.494
there are three candidates

00:06:17.494 --> 00:06:19.888
that are kind of in the lead

00:06:19.888 --> 00:06:21.948
in terms of being furthest along,

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:25.357
and they're all three,
in the middle of large

00:06:25.357 --> 00:06:27.131
phase three clinical trials,

00:06:27.131 --> 00:06:29.518
which is the important, you know,

00:06:29.518 --> 00:06:32.158
kinda final, important phase of a trial.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:36.321
If those candidates look like
they're safe and effective

00:06:36.321 --> 00:06:38.308
at the end of those trials,

00:06:38.308 --> 00:06:40.988
that's when we would begin to start

00:06:40.988 --> 00:06:43.008
using the vaccine on the public,

00:06:43.008 --> 00:06:44.048
but not before that.

00:06:44.048 --> 00:06:47.168
It would be unsafe to do that beforehand,

00:06:47.168 --> 00:06:48.838
and the US won't do that.

00:06:48.838 --> 00:06:50.990
I have confidence that
the US won't do that.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:54.348
There is pressure on the
system, you can feel it.

00:06:54.348 --> 00:06:55.508
If you read the newspaper,

00:06:55.508 --> 00:06:57.618
you can see that there is pressure

00:06:57.618 --> 00:06:59.958
to move as quickly as we can,

00:06:59.958 --> 00:07:02.974
but I do think that
the regulatory agencies

00:07:02.974 --> 00:07:05.144
are gonna follow the right path

00:07:05.144 --> 00:07:07.628
and make sure the trials are completed

00:07:07.628 --> 00:07:08.758
and we know it's safe and effective

00:07:08.758 --> 00:07:10.061
before we use the vaccine.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.278
- And I really want to understand,

00:07:12.278 --> 00:07:13.708
I want folks listening to understand,

00:07:13.708 --> 00:07:15.875
kind of the pros and cons of this.

00:07:15.875 --> 00:07:19.658
So where we are with these
three potential vaccines,

00:07:19.658 --> 00:07:22.178
and it seems like there's
many coming down the pipeline,

00:07:22.178 --> 00:07:23.378
is we're entering phase three.

00:07:23.378 --> 00:07:25.518
Phase three is these large-scale tests

00:07:25.518 --> 00:07:28.408
to once further validate that
people are getting antibodies,

00:07:28.408 --> 00:07:31.248
that they're actually
getting immunity in some form

00:07:31.248 --> 00:07:33.828
or protections against the virus,

00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:35.158
and that it's also safe.

00:07:35.158 --> 00:07:39.374
What do you see as the downsides
of, let's say, you know,

00:07:39.374 --> 00:07:41.128
several of these phase three trials,

00:07:41.128 --> 00:07:42.578
I believe were already, you know,

00:07:42.578 --> 00:07:45.638
several weeks into it or
a month or more into it.

00:07:45.638 --> 00:07:46.928
What if they're already seeing,

00:07:46.928 --> 00:07:48.208
hey a lot of antibodies,

00:07:48.208 --> 00:07:51.078
and we're not seeing people
have some weird side effects,

00:07:51.078 --> 00:07:53.941
what is the negative of, of
moving forward with them?

00:07:55.549 --> 00:07:58.295
- Well, the negative is that we could,

00:07:58.295 --> 00:08:01.016
people could have very
serious adverse reactions

00:08:01.016 --> 00:08:02.218
to the vaccine.

00:08:02.218 --> 00:08:03.566
I think early on,

00:08:03.566 --> 00:08:08.566
these trials will include
up to 30,000 people each.

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:12.591
And we know from other vaccines
that serious reactions from

00:08:12.591 --> 00:08:15.528
vaccines can sometimes
occur at a frequency

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:19.842
that's much less common than
one in 30,000 or one in 10,000.

00:08:19.842 --> 00:08:23.650
Sometimes the more serious
vaccine side effects

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:27.798
take many people to expose

00:08:27.798 --> 00:08:30.358
and so it's really important to be careful

00:08:30.358 --> 00:08:32.418
and not to make judgments on the basis

00:08:32.418 --> 00:08:34.486
of a few hundred people
or a thousand people,

00:08:34.486 --> 00:08:37.628
and to get as much vaccine
safety information as possible.

00:08:37.628 --> 00:08:42.068
We also could have a signal
early on that suggests

00:08:42.068 --> 00:08:43.768
the vaccine is working,

00:08:43.768 --> 00:08:46.218
but when enough people are studied,

00:08:46.218 --> 00:08:48.938
it becomes clear that that
was a matter of chance.

00:08:48.938 --> 00:08:50.788
And we certainly don't
want to begin to vaccinate

00:08:50.788 --> 00:08:52.818
a large number of people with a vaccine

00:08:52.818 --> 00:08:55.918
that doesn't work and, or isn't safe.

00:08:55.918 --> 00:08:59.198
And so I think there's
pretty strong unanimity

00:08:59.198 --> 00:09:00.258
in the public health community

00:09:00.258 --> 00:09:03.178
that these trials are
moving along quickly.

00:09:03.178 --> 00:09:05.198
Hopefully they will
begin to show the results

00:09:05.198 --> 00:09:06.548
over the course of the fall

00:09:07.458 --> 00:09:10.299
that show that it's safe and effective.

00:09:10.299 --> 00:09:12.918
And then we can get onto
the business of vaccinating,

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:14.058
but we shouldn't be doing that before.

00:09:14.058 --> 00:09:17.010
This is a vaccine that will go into

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:21.108
potentially millions, tens of
millions of healthy people.

00:09:21.108 --> 00:09:23.558
And so we really gotta
be sure that we know

00:09:23.558 --> 00:09:25.418
what's in this vaccine, we know it's safe,

00:09:25.418 --> 00:09:28.268
we know it's gonna work before
we move in that direction.

00:09:29.548 --> 00:09:30.978
- I mean, it makes, it
makes a ton of sense.

00:09:30.978 --> 00:09:32.588
I mean, have there been cases,

00:09:32.588 --> 00:09:33.548
I'm sure there are,

00:09:33.548 --> 00:09:36.628
coz phase three trials are
designed for this purpose

00:09:36.628 --> 00:09:38.308
where things looked pretty promising

00:09:38.308 --> 00:09:40.458
at the early parts of
the phase three trial.

00:09:40.458 --> 00:09:43.028
And then as you got into month
three or month four of it,

00:09:43.028 --> 00:09:44.581
I don't know how long they typically last,

00:09:44.581 --> 00:09:46.668
but as you get into
the later stages of it,

00:09:46.668 --> 00:09:47.618
they say, "oh, wow,"

00:09:47.618 --> 00:09:50.418
you know, "one out of a hundred
people are getting XYZ."

00:09:51.758 --> 00:09:52.591
- Yeah, sure.

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:54.808
There've been plenty of
cases where it took some time

00:09:54.808 --> 00:09:57.136
before the adverse
effects began to show up.

00:09:57.136 --> 00:10:01.700
In the way one good part of trials

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.548
or one really important component of it

00:10:04.548 --> 00:10:07.076
is something called the data
safety monitoring board,

00:10:07.076 --> 00:10:09.530
which has set up at the
beginning of the trial

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:14.106
and which peaks into the
data, somewhere along the way.

00:10:14.106 --> 00:10:16.357
And they decide ahead of time.

00:10:16.357 --> 00:10:18.682
Once we get our first hundred cases

00:10:18.682 --> 00:10:21.618
of COVID in our study participants,

00:10:21.618 --> 00:10:23.978
we're gonna peek into the data,

00:10:23.978 --> 00:10:25.444
just this small group of people.

00:10:25.444 --> 00:10:26.828
And we're going to look at it.

00:10:26.828 --> 00:10:29.061
If it looks like the
vaccine is so effective,

00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:32.197
that it would be unethical to continue

00:10:32.197 --> 00:10:35.368
that it's just, we need to
give this vaccine to people.

00:10:35.368 --> 00:10:37.898
It is so incredibly
effective and appears safe.

00:10:37.898 --> 00:10:40.138
They'll stop the trial and
that'll be the end of that.

00:10:40.138 --> 00:10:42.950
And then we'll move on to,
you know, FDA deliberations

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.923
and they'll review the
information, move on.

00:10:45.923 --> 00:10:47.708
Similarly, if they look at the data,

00:10:47.708 --> 00:10:51.092
the first 100 cases of COVID
that occur in the trial,

00:10:51.092 --> 00:10:53.708
and they say, this is really unsafe.

00:10:53.708 --> 00:10:55.268
There's a safety signal here.

00:10:55.268 --> 00:10:57.118
This is not working as planned.

00:10:57.118 --> 00:10:58.283
They'll stop the trial.

00:10:58.283 --> 00:11:00.608
So we do have a check along the way

00:11:00.608 --> 00:11:03.928
to make sure something isn't
so overwhelmingly favorable

00:11:03.928 --> 00:11:05.332
or overwhelmingly unfavorable.

00:11:05.332 --> 00:11:08.438
But if it just looks like
the study needs to continue,

00:11:08.438 --> 00:11:10.388
it's not at one of those two extremes,

00:11:10.388 --> 00:11:11.798
they'll close the data back up.

00:11:11.798 --> 00:11:13.818
They won't say a word about any of it,

00:11:13.818 --> 00:11:15.688
and they'll let the trial continue.

00:11:15.688 --> 00:11:17.648
And then we'll look at the
results when it's completed.

00:11:17.648 --> 00:11:20.198
And that probably will
be sometime this fall.

00:11:20.198 --> 00:11:23.285
By the time there are enough patients,

00:11:23.285 --> 00:11:27.272
for this trial to work, enough
people have to get COVID

